  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For a given array BBB of length MMM, a non-negative integer XXX is said to be **good** if:\n\n\nThe array CCC of length MMM defined as Ci=Bi&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;XC_i = B_i\\space \\&amp;\\space XCi​=Bi​&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;X is sorted in **non-decreasing** order, where &amp;\\&amp;&amp; denotes the Bitwise AND operation.\nGiven an array AAA of length NNN, where 0≤Ai≤N0 \\leq A_i \\leq N0≤Ai​≤N holds true for all iii, count the number of **good** XXX such that 0≤X≤N0 \\leq X \\leq N0≤X≤N.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the number of elements of the array AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space separated integers — the elements of the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of **good** XXX such that 0≤X≤N0 \\leq X \\leq N0≤X≤N.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤5∗1051 \\leq N \\leq 5*10^51≤N≤5∗105",
      "0≤Ai≤N0 \\leq A_i \\leq N0≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 5∗1055*10^55∗105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n0 3 2 \n4\n0 4 1 1 \n10\n9 1 0 2 2 10 4 7 6 7",
        "output": "2\n4\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : The valid XXX are 000 and 222.\n\n\nX=0X = 0X=0 : The sequence CCC is simply [0,0,0][0, 0, 0][0,0,0] which is sorted.\n\n\nX=2X = 2X=2 : The sequence CCC is [0,2,2][0, 2, 2][0,2,2] which is sorted."
      }
    ]
  },
